Prerequisites now: curl, jq, ssh (all pre-installed on macOS)

Install:

chmod +x ~/cli-ss
# Put it somewhere on PATH:
cp ~/cli-ss ~/bin/cli-ss   # (add ~/bin to PATH in ~/.zshrc if needed)
Setup:

export SS_HOST="https://your-secret-server.example.com/ss"
export SS_USER="your-username"
export SS_PASS="your-password"
Use:

cli-ss auth login          # interactive login
cli-ss search webserver    # find secrets
cli-ss ssh webserver       # SSH (password, no sshpass)
cli-ss ssh-key webserver   # SSH (private key from secret)
